WEBVTT

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.490
Independent Unit 8, huh?

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.060
You can do it, Namie!

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:02.170
Someday, in this space deprived of hope,
kono takaki mubou no kuu de itsuka

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:06.840
you'll kneel of your own will.
sono ishi wa hiza wo tateru

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.060
break up foreordination

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.940
Was that flame an illusion or a friend?
fake ano hi wa nakama ka

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:27.650
Am I to venture into the darkness?
susumu beki wa yami ka

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:36.950
You'll find nameless emotions beyond the protruding knife.
knife tsukitateta saki ni shoutai no mienu kanjou

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:42.790
I can't let this end here yet.
ima wa mada koko de owarenai

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.920
I need to get ready to survive.
naraba ikiru junbi wo shiro yo

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:53.220
The passion in my heart only burns hotter.
uzu takaku tsumiageteku netsujou

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:56.720
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:57.770
wake up your tough intention
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:58.180
wake up your tough intention

00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:59.140
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
wake up your tough intention

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:03.400
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:10.030
I'll show you what I've got, bit by bit,
hitotsu zutsu tashikamete yaru kara

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:11.570
so bring it on.
kakattekoi

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.080
break up foreordination

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.870
Blue and Indigo
Blue and Indigo

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.220
Adjust right +3.
Blue and Indigo
Blue and Indigo

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:31.840
Adjust right +3.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.850
Adjust sight, right +3.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.920
Adjust -1.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.480
Adjust sight, -1.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.190
Sight adjustment complete.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.990
How do you like the new gun?

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:52.220
It's made specifically for Argevollen.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:55.480
That makes it accurate and easy to use.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.920
And Argevollen's in great shape after its full tune-up.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:07.710
This may not be the time, but your sister...

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.090
Sorry, did you say something?

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.050
Nothing.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:20.600
I'll get us something to drink.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.690
Hurry up.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:25.020
We've still got the functionality tests.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.610
I know that.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.360
Um, excuse me...

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.970
This is Independent Unit 8, right?

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:41.370
That's right.

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.710
I'm Private Namie Portman.

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:47.380
As of today, I'm joining Unit 8, too.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:51.660
I'm Jamie Hazaford.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:52.880
I'm a civilian engineer.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:58.640
This is my first transfer, so I'm a little nervous.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:02.620
Are you the pilot of the Seiran?

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:03.390
Yes!

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:07.380
But I still don't have a lot of combat experience,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:11.280
so I don't know if the people of Unit 8 will accept me.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.280
Don't worry.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.280
They're not that weird.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.160
They're a group of aces, aren't they?

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:25.540
I heard it's an ace unit that completes even the most difficult operations.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:31.800
Maybe it'd be better to see for yourself.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.190
Yes, I will.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:35.400
Oh, right...

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.730
Want a lollipop?

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.140
Huh?

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.320
Ah, thanks.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:48.040
Say, I was just thinking how cute you are.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.440
C-Cute? Me?

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:56.030
I'll take you there.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:56.820
Thanks.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:01.370
This is so nice.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.230
So shiny, and not a scratch on her!

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:06.410
It'll get scratched up soon enough.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.370
The latest weapon, huh?

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.090
The ZTK5 Seiran.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:14.150
It's far more powerful than the Kokuyou or Kongou.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:16.030
It can keep up with Argevollen.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.790
It's that good?

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.520
Of course not.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:25.520
Its carbon nanomembrane makes its armor half the thickness and weight of the old armor,

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.860
but just as strong.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.290
And its power is amazing, too.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:32.590
This is the real deal.

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:35.270
If they're giving us the latest tech,

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.440
that means they recognize that we're doing well.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.070
I don't know.

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:43.160
It means the battle is going to get harder.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:44.580
That's right.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.350
Maintenance on that is going to feel great.

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:49.230
Did they send us a manual?

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:50.270
Of course.

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:52.940
The short version fills three cardboard boxes.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:54.160
That many?

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.290
That many.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.430
Huh? Who's that?

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.680
Our new pilot.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:07.000
Private Namie Portman.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.930
I've transferred into Unit 8 as of today.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:11.300
Nice to meet you all.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:14.150
And this is...

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:17.690
It's a girl.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:18.740
So it is.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:20.900
She's young.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:21.990
What's your name?

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.080
Private Namie Portman.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:24.840
I've transferred—

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:25.350
How old are you?

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:26.050
What are your hobbies?

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:26.740
Do you have a boyfriend?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:27.790
You're great!

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:29.410
Do you have a type of guy you like?

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:30.960
Older guys? Younger guys?

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:35.670
W-Want a lollipop?

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:39.050
You're not going to eat it?

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:41.050
What are you doing?

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:42.380
The test hasn't...

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.930
Good timing.

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:46.430
The new pilot is here.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:47.960
Tokimune-senpai!

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:50.460
Namie?

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:54.690
Senpai! I never thought I'd see you here.

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:58.070
So you're the new pilot, Namie?

00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:59.570
You gonna be okay?

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:01.590
I don't want to hear that from you.

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:03.530
You're so silly, Senpai.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.090
Excuse me.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:09.200
I'm Private Namie Portman.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.170
I've transferred into... Unit 8 as of today...

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:14.710
What is it?

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.330
You're getting a little red.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:18.550
Did you do it again?

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:19.960
Tokimune-kun?

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.090
You're acquainted?

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:23.410
Yeah.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:25.740
She was an underclassman in my mobile weapons study course.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.720
We were in different grades, but we get along.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:30.720
You get along, huh?

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:35.480
Senpai, where's the captain?

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:42.240
I think he's in the command vehicle over there.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.340
Then will you take me there?

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:46.700
Sure.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:49.730
Thank you very much, Jamie-san.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:55.210
You sure you want to leave them alone?

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:56.580
Why?

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:00.530
It's so brave of you to pretend nothing happened.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:02.300
You've got a rival now.

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:03.620
What do you mean, a rival?

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.070
It's okay.

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:07.850
We'll always be on your side.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:12.570
The captain's out at the moment.

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.350
He'll be back soon, so wait here.

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:15.470
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.570
I'll be on my way, then.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:20.720
Private Susumu.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:52.650
The Seiran is capable of auto-stabilizing itself even on rough terrain,

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:56.470
which was a problem with older models.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:00.360
So you just have to focus on pulling the trigger, huh?

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:01.400
Huh?

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:05.150
Is the profile for this modeling data...

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:09.260
Yes. I'm the sampling model for its maneuvers.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.660
Ooh! What a nice smile!

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:16.890
You can let us see it!

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:19.650
I thought I deleted that picture.

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:21.440
How cute!

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:25.100
Teshigahara Heavy Industries is the largest weapons manufacturer.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.300
And they used your data as their basis.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.250
You're pretty good, Namie.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.380
No, that's not true.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.930
Now we just have to see what you can do in a real battle.

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:37.310
Right.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.450
This is Lorenz.

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:47.030
No sign of the enemy.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:53.670
Lorenz unit destroyed.

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:56.890
Private Portman is talented, isn't she?

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:57.920
Yes.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.920
You're amazing, Namie!

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:02.790
It's nothing special.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:05.300
The abilities of the Seiran make this possible.

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.050
Keep it up!

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:07.880
Right!

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.430
If a girl does it to me, even getting shot's not so bad!

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:17.310
Even so, you let yourself get fragged <i>twice?</i>

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:20.530
It'd be bad if she got me a third time.

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:25.300
All units, proceed to the next exercise area.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:26.690
Roger.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:30.070
This is looking good, Tokimune!

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:34.700
Private Susumu, you're getting too far ahead.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.010
Sorry, Namie!

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:41.830
It's all right. I'm sorry, too.

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:44.130
I'm not used to being a leader.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:47.380
Is that a complaint at being assigned a buddy?

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:48.890
Not at all!

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:49.870
Let's go, Namie!

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:50.880
Right!

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.200
The enemy will come from the left.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:00.770
There are hills to our right.

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:03.520
There's a height gap that makes it dangerous if they target us.

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:06.180
It's a steep hill there.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.030
A Seiran shouldn't be able to scale it.

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:09.740
You're sure?

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:10.730
Yes.

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:14.870
Namie!

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:25.540
No! That's impossible!

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:28.300
Private Portman has been taken out.

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:35.020
I guess Izumi wants to give his prized newbie a trial by fire.

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:42.050
It seems our job is to put her into battle to train her.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:42.810
Yeah.

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.780
That was extremely well done, Sergeant Appleton.

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.110
Corporal Juliano died twice.

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:56.490
Lorenz Juliano only lives twice, huh?

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.240
Two victories and one loss is excellent.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:03.500
But the problem is the battle you lost.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:04.890
I'm aware.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:10.000
I'm sure you prioritized Private Portman's opinion given her familiarity with the Seiran.

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:14.280
But as platoon leader, it's your job to decide how to interpret that.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:15.100
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:19.420
A bad decision on the battlefield will get you killed.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:22.080
Just count your lucky stars this was a training exercise.

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:25.170
It's my fault!

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:26.120
I...

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:29.610
It's entirely my responsibility.

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:31.280
That's right.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:35.890
Everyone, analyze today's combat and submit a report.

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:45.370
I was an idiot to think I knew everything about the Seiren.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:47.500
I had no idea you could climb such a steep incline.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:50.430
Namie, she's right.

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:52.960
It's my job to decide how to interpret your opinion.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:56.860
I'm sorry, Senpai.

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:06.130
Tokimune's synchro rate has been looking good lately!

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:09.520
I guess he's getting closer to Arge.

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:13.360
I'll have to give him a subtle compliment later.

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:20.110
Subtle! Subtle!

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:21.320
He'll let it go to his head.

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:26.030
Tokimune!

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:28.530
Jamie?

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:31.710
You didn't come to the meeting, did you?

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:34.900
Yeah, it took a while to get the data in order.

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:36.970
Anyway, Tokimune,

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:39.660
it looks like your relationship is going well.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:40.750
It's no good.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:43.890
Sure it is!

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:45.350
You're connected deeply!

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:49.340
That can't be a good connection.

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:50.900
We're not connected deeply at all.

00:13:51.670 --> 00:13:52.780
Really?

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:53.920
Really.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:57.740
I need to know exactly what they're thinking.

00:13:57.740 --> 00:14:01.490
Yeah, you need to use them like your own hands or legs.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:03.970
No, that's going too far.

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:08.040
Well, even if we can't be of one mind and body,

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:10.520
I'd still like them to trust me that much.

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:14.000
Yeah, let's both of us keep at it until that happens!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:14.750
Huh?

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:16.250
Huh?

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:20.260
But Namie's got nothing to do with you, Jamie.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:24.150
Oh, yeah... You're right.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:27.320
I was talking about Arge!

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:55.220
I'm no good.

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:57.500
When something not covered in the manual happens,

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:58.760
I can't react.

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:03.260
No battle ever follows the manual.

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:06.770
You froze when that first shot hit you in the shoulder,

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:08.890
but you could've easily kept dodging.

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:15.650
Can I fight a real battle like this?

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.530
I can't answer that.

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.040
It's much more nerve-wracking.

00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:23.160
Real bullets are scary.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.660
How can you fight when you're scared?

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:30.660
Because I'm piloting Argevollen, I guess.

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:36.140
Whenever I'm piloting it, I feel good,

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:38.610
and I feel like I can do anything.

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:41.130
Like it's an extension of my own body.

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:47.680
Will I ever be able to be like that with the Seiran?

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:53.560
Even if I think I'm protected in the Seiran, I'm scared.

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:56.530
You can be scared.

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:58.960
You're not alone when you're fighting.

00:15:58.960 --> 00:15:59.990
You have your companions.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:03.260
That's right!

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:07.870
I'll practice more so I can support you!

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:09.620
Okay, five kilometers left!

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:10.270
Right!

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:43.300
Is she gonna be okay?

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:45.430
She screwed up in the practice fight.

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:47.370
You know what they say.

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:49.870
The battlefield is the best place to train.

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:53.290
But we've had nothing to do lately.

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:56.690
If you keep talking like that, we'll find ourselves with something to do.

00:16:58.630 --> 00:16:59.500
Emergency alert!

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:01.420
See?

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.680
Are you sure?

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:11.680
Isn't it dangerous to put Private Portman into battle?

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:14.060
My decision remains unchanged.

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:22.090
The point is Alpha-12-Zebra.

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:23.230
They aren't moving.

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:24.610
Roger.

00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:25.990
You ready?

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:28.200
Namie, you understand, right?

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:29.870
We're doing rear support this time.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:31.170
Yes.

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:31.740
Let's go.

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:36.370
The operation has begun.

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:40.040
He's over 50%!

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:41.000
Looking good.

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:28.300
No battle ever follows the manual, Namie!

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:02.000
Namie!

00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:24.040
Senpai!

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:26.240
Namie, are you okay?

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:26.990
Yes!

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:30.550
The enemy forces have withdrawn.

00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:32.060
Operation complete.

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:33.920
We're going to withdraw, as well.

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:42.080
It was just for a moment,

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:45.180
but the linkage depth went over 70%!

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:46.190
Amazing!

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:53.190
Thank you!

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:57.700
If it weren't for you, I'd have...

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:58.820
No.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:01.450
You were able to adapt to the battlefield, too.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:03.830
That's thanks to you!

00:21:04.190 --> 00:21:07.690
With some more experience, you'll be able to react better.

00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:10.460
Listen to you, Senpai-kun.

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:16.300
When I saved Namie, I finally understood

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:20.220
that you guys had been supporting me the whole time.

00:21:22.850 --> 00:21:25.480
You're so dense, Tokimune-kun.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:29.600
Well, if you understand that, it's worth giving you a leadership position.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:30.480
Yes.

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:34.430
With some more experience, you'll be able to react better.

00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:38.030
S-Stop it!

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:40.620
No, I thought that line was pretty good!

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:42.620
Oh, come on!

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:45.620
What? It was a compliment, right, Sergeant?

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:46.710
No, it wasn't!
What? It was a compliment, right, Sergeant?

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:48.160
You're making fun of me!

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:51.590
I never thought I'd hear you say something like that, though.

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:53.630
You've grown up.

00:21:53.630 --> 00:21:55.780
Give me a break.

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:57.630
Okay, from now on,

00:21:57.630 --> 00:21:59.840
make sure you listen to Tokimune-senpai.

00:23:37.150 --> 00:23:40.110
Ghost
